# Rust
target/

# Binaries
a.out
# Stray `karac build` outputs accidentally committed from the repo root: the
# AOT compiler emits the executable as `<stem>` into the cwd, so building from
# here drops it beside Cargo.toml where `git add -A` sweeps it up.
#
# The entries below are the names that have actually leaked (tup_vec; then
# blockmin/pan/t; then dc/uam, all 2026-07-31). They keep `git status` quiet,
# but they are NOT the guard — the output name is whatever the `.kara` file was
# called, so a name list can only ever catch a repeat offender, never the next
# one. `tests/no_tracked_binaries.rs` is the real backstop: it rejects any
# tracked file carrying executable magic, under the plain `cargo test --all` CI
# job. When a new stray appears, prefer building into a scratch dir
# (`-o /tmp/prog`) over extending this list.
#
# Root-anchored: `t`, `dc` and `pan` are short enough that a bare pattern would
# also ignore any same-named file or directory deeper in the tree.
tup_vec
/blockmin
/pan
/t
/dc
/uam

# IDX
.idx/

# WIP scratch files (uncommitted). The bug tracker is NOT here — it is the
# committed docs/bug-ledger.jsonl (single source of truth); the old gitignored
# bugs.md scratchpad was retired 2026-06-14 (see docs/bug-ledger.md § One tracker).
wip-*.md

# Built example-package binaries. `karac build` / `karac test` inside an
# example package emits `<package-name>` next to its `kara.toml`, so any
# verification run against these leaves an artifact behind. Regenerate with
# `karac build` from the package directory.
examples/game_of_life/game_of_life
examples/elevator_project/elevator_project

# Built bench binaries (reproduce via the bench dir's README; see
# bench/hot_swap_cost/README.md for the hot-swap pair).
bench/hot_swap_cost/tight_call
bench/hot_swap_cost/tight_call_baseline
bench/hot_swap_cost/tight_call_hotswap
bench/hot_swap_cost/moderate_call
bench/hot_swap_cost/moderate_call_baseline
bench/hot_swap_cost/moderate_call_hotswap

# wasm-pack build output for the browser playground (tracker line 703).
# Regenerate via `wasm-pack build --target web --out-dir web/pkg` from
# `playground/`. wasm-pack writes a `*` gitignore inside the directory;
# this entry covers the directory itself so a fresh checkout starts
# without it.
playground/web/pkg/

# Claude Code session tooling (worktrees, local settings, scratch). Never
# committed — the .claude/worktrees/ tree in particular must not land in the repo.
.claude/

# Self-hosted compiler binary built from the in-tree .kara sources — a local
# build artifact, not source. Regenerate by compiling the self-host entrypoint.
nbe_main
# bench/compile_speed run artifacts (corpus binaries + per-run measurements;
# baseline.json IS tracked — it's the committed gate reference)
bench/compile_speed/synthetic
bench/compile_speed/synthetic_rs
bench/compile_speed/seed_kata
bench/compile_speed/seed_kata_rs
bench/compile_speed/latest.json
bench/compile_speed/gate.md
# Written by the main leg's refresh step (compare.py --drift-out, PR body).
bench/compile_speed/drift.md
bench/compile_speed/pr-body.md

# Python bytecode caches (bench/mend/scripts helpers).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
